author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 120
acceptance_criteria: Public SDK resolver uses installed canonical identity and refuses ambiguity; CLI JSON and text recommend inspection while preserving usage failure; real nonempty source and packed npx/bunx controls preserve authoritative bytes; existing discovery behavior and generated surface gates remain intact
goal: project management = context management
objective: Make a refused namespace mistake recoverable without guessing or executing a mutation
value: Agents discover the intended registered command from a concise executable refusal
why_now: Published 2026.10.10 reproducibly omits canonical update help for item update
parent: pm-f05lsg
risk: low
confidence: high
resolution: "Add a pure public SDK resolver for an unambiguous misplaced namespace suffix, prioritize its registered canonical command in CLI recovery and emit executable canonical help tokens. Keep unknown and ambiguous requests refused and preserve ordinary discovery behavior."
expected_result: "A misplaced item update request remains an error but points to registered update help, with no mutation and no guessed ambiguous or unavailable route."
actual_result: Linked17-test recovery checks and post-extraction144 focused tests passed. Final installed npm/npx and Bun/bunx receipts prove both refused namespace forms preserve authoritative item/history bytes and canonical help resolves. Nine packages and the SDK consumer pass. Every static component passes without budget inflation; the broader recovery census stays explicitly incomplete under its parent.
